<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Protexa places $90 mln promissory notes.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Protexa places $90 mln promissory notes.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private Mexican construction company Protexa Construcciones placed $90 million in five-year promissory notes, the company said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said the notes were the first of some $300 million in debt to be issued under a debt prepayment program.</p>
<p>The $90 million in notes had a maturity of five years including a two-year grace period. The company did not mention what rate the notes carried.</p>
<p>((--Jacqueline Lerma, Monterrey bureau +528 345-7677))</p>
